Z||000003||stimpy||04-05-2001||12:24 PM||||I want one. Badly. <BR>My dad used to have a 67 Mini 1000. That car was a BLAST to ride around in, and it would carry 4 guys 6'+ relatively comfortably. I do like the idea of 4 wheel drive.  Does anyone know if there is a kit for the originl mini? Hmmm, I do have that 323 GTX in my backyard. A mini with 153 hp, all wheel drive & 4 wheel disc brakes! That would be a screamer. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||william_thorniii||04-05-2001||12:35 PM||||I have checked them out thoroughly at the Detroit Int'l Auto Show.  In fact, the Mini was the only car that I wanted to see at the show.  They look nice in pictures and even better in person.  My only problem with them is how well the public embraced them.  They were this years favorite display... which puts them in a crowd with the new beetle and PT cruiser from the last two years.  I still am excited about their release, but if they are anything like other BMW vehicles they will not be available anywhere near their base price.  <P>The driving position is nice.  The seats were comfortable with ample bolstering to hold you in place.  The shifter throw was short and smooth (not like a Miata).  The interior in general had a somewhat cheap feel to it.  I think what I did not like was all of the silver painted plastic pieces (at the bottom of the center pod, on the doors, etc.).  I imagine that the central mounted speedo will cause many a ticket for the folks with autos.  <P>The exterior is beautiful.  I can't wait to see a bright red one with the optional union jack on the roof.  My prediction:  They will be back ordered for the first two years of production.  If you can actually get one for base price, it will INCREASE in value as a lightly used vehicle.  <P>I am excited to see that Cincinnati will get a dealership...<P>William T. Thorn, III<BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||04-05-2001||02:51 PM||||PT Cruiser and New Beetle are the two cars that came to my mind right away when I saw the picture of the New Mini.  I'll say right here, that I am very glad to see there's a market for unique, cool-looking vehicles!!!<BR>||||reg||14
